or sent. No Azure. No spend.**

## HOLDS
No path outside the seven owned paths; no file added, deleted or renamed; no write to `<repo>` or to another lane's `.tools/b*/**`; no pull request; no push to `main`; no force-push; **no rebase, no merge, no amend, no reset**; never delete; no cd; **no `.csproj`, no `packages.lock.json`, no package; no public member changed in `Datasec.Suite.SignIn`, the Universal Print `Registration` folder or `Datasec.Suite.Secrets` (`surface_f1.py` rc 0); no new `TapOutcome` or `RegistrationError` member; no line in `Datasec.Suite.slnx`, `Directory.Packages.props` or `.github/workflows/ci.yml`; no file under `build/**`, `src/Datasec.Suite.Secrets/**`, `src/Datasec.Suite.Sessions/**` or `src/Datasec.Suite.Server/**`; no change to `FLOOR`; no existing case, helper or assertion changed, loosened, skipped or removed (`Kit`'s constructor gains one optional parameter and nothing else); no real-time wait, sleep, retry, platform condition or environment switch added; no configuration file, ignore file, inline allow comment or narrowing option for the secret scan**; a mutant is never committed; no probe file of the drafter's or a gate's is copied into `<clone>`; no download of an SDK or a tool; no `sudo`, `brew`, `apt-get`; **no test selector: every run is a test executable whole or the whole solution, and a total of 0 is a STOP**; no git identity override; no Jira call; no real or real-looking card, user, object id, token or name in any file; no value printed in STATUS, a log or a test's output; no read of a sibling project, of `Source_Documents/`, of any key folder or of the NAS library; no write to `<project>/CLAUDE.md`, `CLARIFICATIONS.md`, `Design`, `Analysis`, `Review`, `BACKLOG.md`, the runbook or the history file; STATUS and a HANDOVER are built and encoded in full first, written to a temp file beside the target, then `os.replace`d, never opened for writing before the content exists, and never encoded whole as ASCII when they already hold non-ASCII bytes (encode the ADDED bytes and check them; then `cmp` the prefix against a before-copy); no hosted call beyond the named exceptions; no az, `docker`, `ssh` of your own; **no text anywhere that says the product owner decided, ruled or approved anything about this lane; no new customer-facing word: the README texts are for engineers.**

## Questions with defaults (Tuesday answers at the stamp; every default is already assumed above)
- **Q1 (D4, the same-object renewal; STOP-CLASS: S4 answers it in words).** Default **a**: refuse it in `Finish` as `Failed` with `TokenAnswerRefused`, the held object kept as it is (not disposed, not re-held, its age not reset), so it is served while less than its whole lifetime has passed and refused after (T13; MEASURED in the drafter's prototype; red under three mutants). Alternative **b**: take it as a renewal (no dispose, the age reset): it makes an old token look fresh for a whole new lifetime; `mSameObjectAccepted` is this alternative and T13 is red under it (MEASURED). Alternative **c**: copy every answer's bytes into a token the holder makes itself, then dispose the answer: not built; it changes the ownership rule of `ICloudDeviceTokenIssuer.cs:9`, a second same-object answer would then be refused by the disposed check, and an issuer that clears its answer between the check and the copy still hands over cleared bytes (DERIVED). Cost of a: none beyond the built patch; a buggy issuer's renewals keep failing until the held token's lifetime ends.
- **Q2 (D2, the empty identifier; STOP-CLASS: S4 answers it in words).** Default **a**: `LookupFailed` at the card user's object id, nothing acquired, no audit (B09, B10). Alternative **b**: let the lookup pass and refuse at the binding rule as `BindingRefused` with one audit (an acquire is made first, the printer is told; the audit records it); not built (+1 line at `:346`, B09 and B10 rewritten). Alternative **c**: both (the `:346` line is then never reached: DERIVED, an equivalent mutant). Cost of a: a defective identity service's empty answer leaves no audit record, only `LookupFailed` to the caller.
- Q3 (D1, the fan-out). Default: each handler in its own try, in subscription order, one shared arguments object. Alternative: a fresh arguments object per handler (no difference while the type is immutable). Cost: none known.
- Q4 (D3, the two Limits lines). Default: named in the README, not asserted (probes P1 and P2 measured each once). Alternative: two limit cases of those shapes (+2 cases; not built).
- Q5 (D4's named limit in the Universal Print README: an issuer that keeps and later clears a token it handed over, or answers with a holder copy). Default: named only (probes Q1, Q2). Alternative: also refuse an answer whose `Origin` is set (a copy the holder itself handed out), +1 line and +1 case, not built; it does not reach an issuer that keeps and clears its own token (DERIVED).
- Q6 (the level). Default: Opus by `<project>/CLAUDE.md:7`, `BRIEF_SEAT_LEVEL=opus`. Alternative: Sonnet (the routing row C2; against the project's rule).
- Q7 (D6, windows and pane). Default: no rebase (the gate reads the merge); READY at Step 0 + 120 minutes, the push by Step 0 + 90, pane `Datasec/OXPd2-X37`, 30 minutes of lock waits; gate G1 round 1, Opus. Alternative: rebase the unpushed commit onto a moved `main` before the push (then the hosted totals are that `main`'s plus 6, which the seat would have to read first).

